data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":"{\"kind\":\"constraints\",\"title\":\"Constraints: Animated Weather App\",\"content\":\"## In short\\n- A **website that works in any browser**, on desktop and phone, and can be added to a home screen.\\n- Runs on **free weather and city-search services**, with **no sign-in** and **no cost to you** to run at first.\\n- **Smooth animation on mid-range phones**, with a reduce-motion option and text that stays readable.\\n- First version covers the standard weather features; **radar, alerts, accounts and native apps wait**.\\n\\n## Solution form\\nA hosted website (the brief: \\\"works in a browser on desktop and phone\\\"). It can be installed to a phone or computer home screen so it feels like an app. Left out: native iPhone/Android apps, because they need app-store accounts, fees and separate builds, and the brief only asks for a browser.\\n\\n## Platforms and devices\\n- Current versions of Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge, on desktop and phone (the brief).\\n- Layout adapts from small phone screens to wide desktop screens (the brief's success criteria).\\n- Animations must stay smooth on a mid-range phone, so the visuals are kept light enough for that.\\n\\n## People and scale\\nPeople who check the weather regularly (the brief). No user count was given, so we plan for personal or small-audience use. Nobody needs to create an account or install anything beyond a browser.\\n\\n## Data sources\\n- **Weather:** a free forecast service that needs no account, such as Open-Meteo. It supplies current conditions, hourly and multi-day forecasts, feels-like, wind and humidity (the brief).\\n- **City search:** a free city-lookup service, turning typed names into places.\\n- **Your location:** the browser's own location feature, used only when you allow it.\\n- **Saved data:** your saved cities and °C/°F choice are kept in your own browser on that device. They are not shared between devices.\\n\\n## Privacy and accessibility\\n- No sign-in, and we keep no user database (the brief).\\n- The only location data is your device location, requested with permission, and the city names you search. Both go only to the weather and city-lookup services to fetch results.\\n- If you decline location, the app still works through city search.\\n- The animations follow the device's \\\"reduce motion\\\" setting by switching to calm or still visuals (the brief).\\n- Text and numbers stay readable over animated backgrounds, with enough contrast, and the app can be used with a keyboard and screen reader.\\n\\n## Outside services and accounts\\n- Weather service and city-lookup service: both free, with no account or key from you.\\n- Hosting: a simple, low-cost or free static web host. You may need to create one account for it when we publish.\\n\\n## Budget and timeline\\nNo budget or date was given. We assume the lowest cost: free data services and minimal hosting, so running cost is zero or close to it. Free services have usage limits and can change terms, which is the main risk of this choice.\\n\\n## First version and later\\n**Included:** current conditions; hourly and multi-day forecast; °C/°F toggle; current location; search, save and remove cities; compare two or more saved cities; weather-driven animated look (rain, snow, wind, heat and more).\\n\\n**Later, with reasons:**\\n- Radar maps: heavy to build and need a different data source (the brief).\\n- Severe weather alerts: need reliable official data and care to get right (the brief).\\n- Accounts and syncing across devices: not needed for the first version.\\n- Native apps: see Solution form.\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Open-Meteo for weather, as it is free and needs no key; if it falls short we swap to another free service.\\n- A free city-lookup service (Open-Meteo's own city search) so there is one provider.\\n- Low budget, minimal hosting on a free static host.\\n- \\\"Mid-range phone\\\" means a phone from roughly the last four to five years.\\n- Installable to the home screen, but it needs internet for fresh weather; it may show the last data seen when offline.\\n- Accessibility aims at the common WCAG 2.2 AA level for contrast and keyboard use.\\n- Saved cities live only in the browser, so clearing browser data removes them.\\n\\n## Open questions\\nNone. The brief gave no bounds, so everything above is an assumption for you to correct.\\n\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

